<main class="sec" style="padding-top:52px">
  <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1 class="coll__h1">Policies</h1>
  <p class="coll__lede">Written for a made-to-order brand, not copied from a template. Last updated {{ section.settings.updated }}.</p>

  <div class="divider" style="padding:26px 0 0"><div class="tilat-rule tilat"></div></div>

  <div class="faq">
    <details id="refund" open>
      <summary><span class="faq__n">01</span>Refund policy</summary>
      <div class="faq__body">
        <p>Every MEQENET piece is printed and sewn after you order it. Nothing is held in stock, which means a returned garment cannot be resold. Our policy is built around that.</p>
        <p><strong>Damaged, defective or misprinted.</strong> If your order arrives damaged, misprinted, or materially different from what was shown, write to us within 30 days of delivery with a photograph of the item and of the packing slip. We will remake and reship it at no cost, or refund it in full, whichever you prefer. You do not need to send the original back.</p>
        <p><strong>Lost in transit.</strong> If tracking shows no movement for ten business days, or shows delivery to an address you did not enter, contact us and we will remake the order.</p>
        <p><strong>Wrong size ordered.</strong> Because the piece was made to your selection, a size change is not a defect. Contact us within 30 days and we will work something out in good faith, though we cannot promise a free replacement. The size guide on the Contact page is the best way to avoid this.</p>
        <p><strong>Change of mind.</strong> Email us within two hours of ordering and we can usually cancel before production begins. Once production has started the piece exists only for you and cannot be cancelled.</p>
        <p><strong>Incorrect address.</strong> If a parcel returns to us because the address was wrong or incomplete, we will reship once you confirm the correct address. Reshipping is charged at cost.</p>
        <p><strong>How refunds are issued.</strong> Approved refunds return to the original payment method. Your bank or card issuer controls the timing, typically five to ten business days after we process it.</p>
        <p><strong>Sale items and gift cards.</strong> Sale items follow this same policy. Gift cards are not refundable.</p>
        <p><strong>How to start.</strong> Use the form on the Contact page, or reply to your order confirmation email. Include your order number.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="shipping">
      <summary><span class="faq__n">02</span>Shipping policy</summary>
      <div class="faq__body">
        <p><strong>Production time.</strong> Two to five business days for printed apparel and accessories. Embroidered items can take one to two days longer. Production time is separate from transit time, and orders placed on a weekend begin production the next business day.</p>
        <p><strong>Transit time.</strong> Domestic orders typically arrive three to five business days after shipping. International orders vary widely by destination, commonly ten to twenty business days.</p>
        <p><strong>Rates.</strong> Shipping is calculated at checkout from your address and the contents of your order. The amount shown at checkout is the amount charged.</p>
        <p><strong>Tracking.</strong> A tracking link is emailed the moment your order ships. Carriers can take 24 to 48 hours to show the first scan; a link that looks inactive at first is normal.</p>
        <p><strong>Split shipments.</strong> Orders containing several item types may be produced in different facilities and arrive separately, at no extra charge to you.</p>
        <p><strong>Customs, duties and import taxes.</strong> International orders may attract import duties and taxes set by the destination country and collected by the carrier on delivery. These charges are not ours, are not included in your order total, and cannot be refunded by us. Refused parcels returning to us are treated as an incorrect-address case.</p>
        <p><strong>Where we ship.</strong> Anywhere Shopify checkout accepts an address for this store. If your country does not appear at checkout, we cannot currently ship there.</p>
        <p><strong>Delays.</strong> Weather, customs inspections and peak-season carrier volume can add time beyond these estimates. We will tell you what we know if you ask.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="privacy">
      <summary><span class="faq__n">03</span>Privacy policy</summary>
      <div class="faq__body">
        <p>This policy explains what we collect when you visit or buy from this store, why, and what you can ask us to do about it.</p>
        <p><strong>What we collect.</strong> When you place an order: your name, billing and shipping address, email, phone number if given, and the contents of your order. Payment card details go directly to our payment processor and are never stored by us or visible to us. When you simply browse: device and browser information, pages viewed, and referring site, collected through cookies. When you join our list or use the contact form: your email address, and whatever you write to us.</p>
        <p><strong>Why we collect it.</strong> To produce and ship your order, to email you about that order, to answer your questions, to detect fraud, and to understand in aggregate which pages people find useful. If you have joined the list, to send occasional news about new work.</p>
        <p><strong>Who we share it with.</strong> Only the services required to run the store: Shopify, which hosts the store and processes payments; our print and fulfilment partner, which receives the name, address and order contents needed to make and ship your parcel; and shipping carriers. We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for advertising purposes.</p>
        <p><strong>Marketing email.</strong> You receive marketing email only if you asked to. Every message carries an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing takes effect immediately.</p>
        <p><strong>Cookies.</strong> The store uses cookies necessary for the cart and checkout to function, plus basic analytics. Blocking cookies in your browser will break the cart.</p>
        <p><strong>How long we keep it.</strong> Order records are kept as long as tax and accounting rules require. Mailing-list addresses are kept until you unsubscribe.</p>
        <p><strong>Your rights.</strong> You may ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Depending on where you live you may also have the right to object to certain processing or to lodge a complaint with a data-protection authority. Write to us and we will respond within 30 days. We will need to verify your identity before acting on a request.</p>
        <p><strong>Children.</strong> This store is not intended for anyone under 16 and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>
        <p><strong>Changes.</strong> If this policy changes materially we will update the date at the top of this page.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="terms">
      <summary><span class="faq__n">04</span>Terms of service</summary>
      <div class="faq__body">
        <p>By using this store or placing an order you agree to what follows.</p>
        <p><strong>The store.</strong> This site is operated by {{ shop.name }}. "We" and "us" mean the business; "you" means the visitor or customer.</p>
        <p><strong>Orders.</strong> Placing an order is an offer to buy, which we may accept or decline. We may decline or cancel an order that appears fraudulent, that we cannot produce, or where a price or description was published in error. If we cancel a paid order we refund it in full.</p>
        <p><strong>Prices and descriptions.</strong> Prices are in the currency shown at checkout and may change without notice. We work to describe products accurately, but colours shown on a screen are approximate and a printed garment will never match a monitor exactly.</p>
        <p><strong>Made to order.</strong> Items are produced after purchase. See the refund policy above for what this means for returns.</p>
        <p><strong>Payment.</strong> Payments are processed by Shopify Payments and the card networks. By submitting payment details you confirm you are authorised to use that method.</p>
        <p><strong>Intellectual property.</strong> All artwork, designs, photographs, the MEQENET name and the Amharic wordmark are owned by us and may not be reproduced, printed, resold or used commercially without written permission. Buying a garment does not transfer any rights in the design on it.</p>
        <p><strong>Your content.</strong> If you send us photographs, ideas or feedback, we may use them to improve the store and, unless you tell us otherwise, may quote a review or repost a photograph you sent us. You keep ownership of what you sent.</p>
        <p><strong>Acceptable use.</strong> Do not use the store unlawfully, attempt to breach its security, scrape it, or resell our products as your own.</p>
        <p><strong>Third-party services.</strong> The store depends on Shopify, our fulfilment partner and shipping carriers. We are not responsible for their independent acts or outages, though we will help you sort out anything that goes wrong with your order.</p>
        <p><strong>Liability.</strong> To the extent the law allows, our liability for any order is limited to the amount you paid for it. We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss. Nothing here limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be limited.</p>
        <p><strong>Governing law.</strong> These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Maryland, United States, without regard to conflict-of-law rules.</p>
        <p><strong>Changes.</strong> We may update these terms. The version on this page at the time you order is the one that applies to that order.</p>
        <p><strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about these terms go through the form on the Contact page.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <p class="legal__note">Written in plain language for a small made-to-order brand. It is not legal advice, and a lawyer in your jurisdiction may want to adjust it.</p>
</main>
